              "cost_adj": "50%",
              "local_notes": "Power cannot be Negated"
            }
          ],
          "local_notes": "**Control (Time) 23**, base 30 points/level:\n\n| Modifier | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Cosmic — Power cannot be Negated | +50% |\n| Ranged | +40% |\n| Reduced Fatigue Cost 1 | +20% |\n| Selective Effect | +20% |\n| Natural Phenomena | +100% |\n| Super-Effort | +400% |\n| **Total enhancements** | **+630%** |\n\n**Cost:** 30 × 23 × 7.30 = **[5,037]**, or **[219/level]**.\n\n| Mode | Effective Control | Maximum radius | Maximum acceleration |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Normal effort | 23 | **2.3 miles** | **×7,864,320** |\n| Super-Effort | 15,000 | **1,500 miles** | **30 × 2^14,995**, approximately **2.64 × 10^4,515** |\n\nTsar's ordinary effort exceeds Aetas's level 15, while his Super-Effort is vastly stronger. The previously discussed approximately ×40,000,000 configuration fits within his Super-Effort range. He can choose a much smaller area, including the earlier six-mile operating radius.\n\nTsar almost never uses the maximum temporal rate for appreciable external time. A domain may exist for substantially less than an outside second while an enormous subjective interval passes within it.\n\n**Selective modifier history:** The supplied workbook and the level-23 audit use **Selective Effect**, retained here. The earlier level-9 discussion used Selective Area at the same +20%. The historical naming difference does not justify purchasing both.",
          "reference": "P90",
          "source": {
            "library": "richardwilkes/gcs_master_library",
            "path": "Powers/Powers Traits.adq",
            "id": "t6PGPHm9Ne6rxNIxG"
          },
          "calc": {
            "points": 5037,
            "current_level": 23
          }
        }
      ],
      "local_notes": "Temporal Domain changes **genuine local elapsed time**. Thought, metabolism, healing, aging, gestation, machinery, spell durations, and actual practice follow local time unless another ability explicitly changes them.\n\nFor effective Control level 5 or more:\n\n**Maximum acceleration = 30 × 2^(effective level − 5).**\n\nThe earlier progression below level 5 was ×2, ×4, ×8, ×15, then ×30 at level 5.\n\nThe September 14 discussion accepted **symmetrical temporal ranges**: the corresponding slow-time limit is the reciprocal of the maximum acceleration. For example, an acceleration cap of ×480 corresponds to a slow-time limit of ×1/480. This is a campaign extension, not a statement that every published Control build has that range.\n\nWith the adopted **Natural Phenomena +100%** treatment:\n\n**Radius = 0.1 × effective Control level, in miles.**\n\nThe user can choose a smaller radius, a less extreme rate, or both. Radius and rate are separate settings within their respective limits.\n\n- **Maintenance:** Continuous concentration is required; Persistent was deliberately omitted.\n- **Fatigue:** Reduced Fatigue Cost 1 removes the specified 1 FP activation expenditure. No recurring FP drain was included in the recovered build.\n- **Boundary normalization:** Crossing changes the subject's local time rate without multiplying velocity, momentum, kinetic energy, or stored energy.\n- **Combat:** This does not confer purchased Altered Time Rate or a free personal allotment of extra combat maneuvers.\n- **Training:** Actual practice may count as study. Merely inserting a memory does not create completed training.\n- **Cosmic:** Tsar's +50% Cosmic is specifically **Power cannot be Negated**, subject to appropriate Cosmic countermeasures; it is not a blanket permission to bypass every rule.",
      "tags": [
        "Settled",
        "Temporal"
      ],
      "calc": {
