        },
        {
          "id": "mkoO-VKiDh4i_YxVM",
          "name": "Summonable",
          "cost_adj": "100%"
        }
      ],
      "local_notes": "The September 7 accepted build:\n\n**Ally, 100% of Tsar's point value [5]**, **Always available ×4**, **Special Abilities +50%**, **Summonable +100%**.\n\n**Cost:** 5 × 4 × 2.50 = **[50]**.\n\nThis was the explicitly accepted Sol Mahina Ally entry; it should not be replaced by a generic family budget.",
      "reference": "B36",
      "calc": {
        "points": 50
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "TV2rHSW2_KqPcW-V7",
      "name": "Campaign Operating Rules",
      "container_type": "meta_trait",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "tlsh5OEIy4eliAgGZ",
          "name": "Remote Embodiment and Parallel Experience",
          "tags": [
            "Sol Mahina"
          ],
          "local_notes": "Operating notes for paid powers; not an independent free ability.\n\nThe corrected sensory direction is:\n\n**Sol's real sensory feed → Tsar's interface/simulation compartment → Tsar's own Mental Illusion → Tsar's experiencing compartment.**\n\nHis intended actions are relayed back for Sol's Illusion/TK manifestation to carry out. Sol supplies the real feed; **Tsar constructs the Mental Illusion he experiences**. For this arrangement, the September discussion allocated two Tsar compartments: interface/simulator and embodied participant.\n\nThis lets one part of Tsar remain personally present with people at home while other compartments handle other activity.\n\nSol's physical realm-body remains in Sol Mahina. A participating Sol compartment experiences Tsar's Mental Illusion as a natural first-person environment. Tsar's real senses provide the feedback, while his external Illusion/TK mirrors Sol's movements and interactions in the real destination.\n\nSol does not manually puppeteer an avatar by issuing detached control commands; she walks and interacts naturally in the experienced environment.\n\nFor the described Tsar-hosted group arrangement:\n\n**N independently embodied companions require N Mental-Illusion compartments + 1 shared external Illusion/TK projection compartment.**\n\n| Companions | Individual mental environments | Shared physical projection | Total Tsar compartments |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | **2** |\n| 4 | 4 | 1 | **5** |\n\nThe shared external suite can present all the group's bodies while the separate mental environments supply individualized perspective. Four companions therefore do **not** automatically require eight Tsar compartments. This count addresses the described simulation/projection work; an end-to-end setup must also accommodate its real sensory feed and any separately needed host activity.\n\nThe travellers' actual bodies remain where they are being hosted. Their projections are manifestations, not relocated biological bodies. Consequences of injury to a manifestation must follow the actual TK, feedback, and Stigmata rules selected for the setup; no universal damage-immunity rule was finalized.",
          "calc": {
            "points": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t1FlcaiQOQcnPWnc0",
          "name": "Conditional Realm Gifts and Personhood",
          "tags": [
            "Sol Mahina"
          ],
          "local_notes": "Operating notes, not a purchased power.\n\n**Established September 4:** Sol Mahina can selectively suspend her gifts from an individual.\n\nThe proposed organizing rule distinguishes:\n\n1. Natural properties of the realm.\n2. Physical infrastructure and services.\n3. Individually bestowed gifts.\n\nPresence in the realm does not automatically confer an irrevocable entitlement to every gift. Gifts may be granted, withheld, suspended, or restored individually. An ability that belongs to the character independently is not automatically reclassified as a realm gift.\n\nA single final Affliction package and universal duration for every realm gift were not recovered.\n\n**Established September 13 choices:**\n\n- Genesis-created material is permanent and independent of Tsar, without a Creation Pool.\n- Negating his ongoing creation ability does not erase already-created permanent matter.\n- Created Functional Minds and awakening an existing subject are different operations.\n- Divine Awakening's first appropriate use establishes personhood/soul; later elevation does not duplicate a soul.\n- Divine Awakening retains Cancellation of Tsar's own gift under the chosen construction.\n- Permanent creation and cancelable bestowed traits therefore need not have identical revocation rules.",
          "calc": {
            "points": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tLKEp1PLnkevLyhkE",
          "name": "Calendar Knowledge after World Travel",
          "tags": [
            "Sol Mahina"
          ],
          "local_notes": "Operating distinction, not free current-date knowledge.\n\n**Established September 17 distinction:** Recognizing a calendar and knowing the present date are different kinds of knowledge.\n\nA character may remember a world's calendar structure but still need an in-world source or an appropriate time-sense capability to establish the current date after travel. A gate clock or a knowledgeable person can supply that information. The group need not use a special GM button as the fictional mechanism.\n\nThe usual Sol Mahina external/local comparison is **100:1**. Its calendar-day notation, local elapsed hours, and time-power ratios should be tracked as distinct quantities; one of those alone does not prove a traveller knows another world's present date.",
          "calc": {
            "points": 0
          }
        }
      ],
      "calc": {
        "points": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "TZVT3l2MkvVY65jUM",
      "name": "Draft Powers and Variable-Cost Recipes",
      "container_type": "meta_trait",
      "children": [
