        {
          "id": "tdL8B3NRnnjf-HFnC",
          "name": "Divine Inspiration — DRAFT",
          "tags": [
            "Draft",
            "Needs Review",
            "Sol Mahina"
          ],
          "disabled": true,
          "local_notes": "INCOMPLETE OR PROPOSED BUILD. Disabled deliberately. A displayed zero is not a free power; finalize the specification and price before use.\n\n**Status:** Established intended behavior; **working price [156]** with incomplete modifier reconciliation.\n\nThe concept is an **Affliction granting Wild Talent with Retention**. The bestowed Wild Talent itself must contain the enhancements needed to produce the intended effects; putting Cosmic only on the delivery Affliction does not automatically enhance its payload.\n\nAccepted development:\n\n- Retention permits learned skills to become permanent purchases.\n- The earlier 30-point/one-level Wild Ability ceiling was intentionally removed.\n- Universal access extends beyond abilities already present in the recipient's power set.\n- Ability Retention extends retention to gained abilities.\n- The recipient may use unspent character points, then **voluntarily take point debt**.\n- The retained ability works immediately; future earned CP repay that debt.\n- Retained abilities survive cancellation of the original Inspiration.\n- Manifestation is personalized to the recipient, and the later working version is fully configurable.\n\nThe recovered payload is **Wild Talent 1**, recorded at **[125]**:\n\n| Named payload modifier | Recorded value |\n|---|---:|\n| Retention | +25% |\n| Perfective | +50% |\n| Unbounded Wild Ability | +100% |\n| Universal Wild Ability | +100% |\n| Ability Retention | +100% |\n| Fully Configurable | +100% |\n| Personalized Manifestation | [0] feature |\n\nThese named modifiers alone yield **[115]**, not [125]. The detailed template adds an explicitly unresolved +50% reconciliation entry to preserve [125]. It likewise preserves the delivery [156] using a +210% remainder beyond the +1,250% payload enhancement. Those remainder entries are **not newly approved modifiers**.\n\n**Accounting:** Purchase the Affliction at its working **[156]**. The displayed [125] payload is a breakdown, not a second purchase; [281] is the erroneous double-counted total.\n\n**Historical stage:** The earlier Wild Talent [65] / Affliction [96] proposal preceded Universal Ability, expanded retention, and full configurability. It does not price the later version.",
          "calc": {
            "points": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tGOycbgnlyRitqh-D",
          "name": "Divine Union — DRAFT",
          "tags": [
            "Draft",
            "Needs Review",
            "Sol Mahina"
          ],
          "disabled": true,
          "local_notes": "INCOMPLETE OR PROPOSED BUILD. Disabled deliberately. A displayed zero is not a free power; finalize the specification and price before use.\n\n**Status:** Established delivery and fertility canon; incomplete consolidated mechanical build.  \n**Sources:** September 4, 9–13, and September 20 clarification.\n\n### Established operation\n\n- Divine Union is a physically delivered **Affliction**, with **Blood Agent** central to its delivery.\n- Conception can overcome species, sex, anatomy, infertility, and ordinary reproductive incompatibility under the intended Cosmic fertility effect, when Tsar intends it and the partner willingly permits it.\n- The effect does not make every species in Sol Mahina mutually fertile by default.\n- The recipient's Affliction (Ecstasy) is distinct from Tsar's own ordinary bodily response; he does not automatically receive his own Affliction.\n- **Emergencies Only −30% was intentional**, tied to the particular intense emotional/physical activation state. It should not be deleted as an assumed mistake.\n- The cited Ecstasy Glands precedent was inspiration for delivery, not permission to import every consequence of that example. The proposed Tsar build did not retain Heart Attack.\n\n### Recovered core mechanics\n\nThe discussion repeatedly used **Affliction 40**, **Based on Will +20%**, **Ecstasy +100%**, **Cumulative +400%**, **Blood Agent −40%**, **Onset — 1 minute −10%**, and close-contact delivery. Duration ×3 was quoted at **+20%**.\n\nTwo custom Cosmic functions were discussed: **reproductive compatibility +300%** and **protection from ordinary negation/countermeasures +50%**.\n\nOther drafts included Cancellation, a healing aftermath, and Fast Regeneration **1 HP/minute**. The recovered versions disagree over Cancellation's valuation and close-contact wording, and the later full aftermath package was not recovered. The older template totals therefore remain historical rather than a new final price.\n\n**Resistance clarification:** The discussed Affliction 40 used a straight **Will−39 resistance roll**, not a Malediction Quick Contest. “No Rule of 16” does not solve that straight resistance roll.\n\nThe recorded duration interpretation was **3 minutes × margin of failure** when applicable to that Affliction build. This is not the default duration of an ordinary climax.\n\n### Conception count and related ideas\n\nA September 12 proposal used a Fertility roll to determine conception outcome/count with a **minimum of one child** when the divine guarantee applies. The exact final count procedure was not recovered, so no die table is invented here.\n\nThe September discussions also treated controlled hybridization, functional intersex reproduction, and possible self-fertilization as dependent on the actual fictional reproductive design and the character's fertility control. No universal percentage chance was agreed.\n\n### Mental simulation boundary\n\nThe September 20 correction explicitly allows genuine bodily responses through the existing Cosmic Mindscape/Stigmata construction, including the discussed healing. Nevertheless, a mental simulation cannot supply Divine Union's physical agent or cause its conception effect without the required physical delivery.\n\nSol's awakening history involved a force construct, full sensory illusion, an actual realm-wide Divine Union event affecting her real realm-body, and a permanently dedicated compartment becoming Sol. That history does not establish a general rule that an arbitrary illusion can become pregnant.\n\n### Technique proposals, not adopted additions\n\n**Tsargoth's Intimate Benediction** was proposed with +4 Stimulation, or +8 on critical success, then set aside after the user noted that incapacitating Ecstasy made those bonuses largely irrelevant.\n\nThe replacement **Perfect Convergence / Divine Echo** proposal was:\n\n- Ordinary success: no added Stimulation.\n- Critical success on the underlying technique and failed Divine Union resistance: normal Ecstasy.\n- Critical success on the underlying technique and successful ordinary resistance: a proposed **three-minute Divine Echo**.\n- Critical resistance: resists completely.\n\nNo acceptance of that replacement was recovered. It is not added as a purchased technique.",
          "calc": {
            "points": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "th3iD2dCXJ8HR8wl8",
          "name": "Divine Spark — DRAFT",
          "tags": [
            "Draft",
            "Needs Review",
            "Sol Mahina"
          ],
          "disabled": true,
          "local_notes": "INCOMPLETE OR PROPOSED BUILD. Disabled deliberately. A displayed zero is not a free power; finalize the specification and price before use.\n\n**Status:** Established concept, expenditure, and recovery decisions; final payload pricing unresolved.  \n**Source:** September 7.\n\nDivine Spark permanently invests divine essence. It can grant new divinity, deepen existing divinity, or restore sealed/stolen divinity. Repeated investment can lead to apotheosis.\n\nThe adopted design direction was **Cumulative +400%**, **Truly Permanent**, and a variable/leveled investment. Repeated transfers build the relevant leveled Spark package, rather than granting duplicate copies of the same nonleveled trait.\n\nThis differs from temporary Divine Union, from awakening personhood, and from simply creating a body.\n\n### Donor expenditure and recovery\n\n**Transfer expenditure:** **95% of maximum FP**. Starting at full FP therefore leaves **5%**.\n\n| Phase | Divine FP regeneration |\n|---|---|\n| During the Spark-induced Ecstasy | **0** |\n| First 24 hours after Ecstasy ends | **1 FP/hour** |\n| Following seven days | **1 FP/minute** |\n| After that recovery period | Normal divine FP regeneration |\n\n**Normal biological/rest-based FP recovery remains available**; the schedule suppresses the separate divine regeneration.\n\nThe accepted HP recovery wording was **1 HP/minute during Ecstasy and through the following week**, instead of Tsar's normal **1 HP/second**, followed by restoration of the normal HP rate.\n\n**Unresolved timing detail:** The HP wording was “after one week,” while the FP schedule explicitly has 24 hours followed by seven days. The recovered discussion does not establish that these endpoints coincide. Keep their original wording rather than silently making both seven or eight days.\n\nThe exact Spark-induced Ecstasy duration, the recipient's priced Spark package, investment limits, and the interaction of later transfers with an unfinished recovery period were not recovered.\n\n### Spark-state telepathy and recording\n\nAn earlier proposal used Telesend/Sensie with Mind Reading/Sensory, Multiple Contacts for up to two others, and short-range/unconscious or uncontrollable operation during the Spark state. The user wanted the partner's experience recorded.\n\nThe later Familiar Bond and Archive now supply much of the broader sharing/recording architecture. A distinct Spark-only telepathy purchase was not finalized in the recovered material and is not charged again here.",
          "calc": {
            "points": 0
          }
        },
